  "transcript": "Canonical serialization rule: take the proposal artifact EXACTLY as given in the prompt, then JSON-serialize it with sorted keys and no whitespace; persist the exact bytes as proposal_canon.json in the run scratch dir, and compute seed = SHA-256(proposal_canon.json). A third party can re-derive by hashing proposal_canon.json with sha256sum to reproduce seedHex, and (per the instance’s salted census mode) by re-deriving hProposal = SHA-256(proposal_canon.json) and then computing seed = SHA-256(hProposal + salt) where salt = 65c00a5d0aabbd8c2ed654e36d9626d9d28c2c87b1a5370d5edb39db3b6d8a0d; the check is mechanical: sha256sum proposal_canon.json equals the seedHex above."
